## internal/app/{{ .Module.Name }}/graphql/schema/directive.graphqls

The new schema uses `@authenticate`{{ if .Entity.UsesPermissions }} and `@hasPermission(permission: String!)`{{ end }}. Declare any that are missing:

```graphql
directive @authenticate on FIELD_DEFINITION
{{- if .Entity.UsesPermissions }}
directive @hasPermission(permission: String!) on FIELD_DEFINITION
{{- end }}
```

and wire them in `graphql/init.go` the way the module already wires its directives.
{{- if .Entity.UsesPermissions }}
`HasPermission` needs core-lib v0.2.0+ (`authdirective.New`); on older core-lib use
`directive.VerifyUserPermission(permission)` behind a small adapter.
{{- end }}
The generated e2e test (`graphql/e2e_{{ .Entity.Snake }}_integration_test.go`) calls
`NewHandler(generated.DirectiveRoot{...})` with pass-through directives. If `graphql/init.go` has no such
seam, split it: `Init` keeps building the real directives from config and returns
`NewHandler(generated.DirectiveRoot{Authenticate: directive.Authenticate(), ...})`; `NewHandler` holds the
rest of the old body (`generated.Config{Resolvers: resolver.NewResolver(), Directives: directives}`,
server, error presenter, `EnrichContext`, loader middleware). Behaviour is unchanged.

Scalars `Time`, `Any` and `Map`, inputs `Filter`, `PageInput`, `Sort` and the enums `FilterOperator`,
`SortOrder` must exist in the module schema. Add whichever are missing from the bootstrap module
templates (`templates/module/.../graphql/schema/`). `graphql/mapper/query_builder.go` must expose
`MapQueryOptionsToQueryBuilder(QueryOptions) *coredto.QueryBuilder`. If the module's version returns
`(*coredto.QueryBuilder, error)`, adapt the generated resolver call instead of changing the module: when
that error is always nil (backend-b, backend-a), `queryBuilder, _ := ...` with a one-line comment keeps
the 100% gate honest; otherwise handle it and add a test that triggers it.
